# Project Architecture

Confiro is a modular monolith EdTech MCQ platform. Read `AGENTS.md` and `docs/04-system-architecture.md` before structural changes.

## Non-negotiable decisions

- Stack is fixed (Next.js + NestJS + Prisma + PostgreSQL + Redis + BullMQ + Cloudinary). Do not swap without approval.
- Modular monolith only — no microservices unless explicitly approved.
- Monorepo: `apps/web`, `apps/api`, `apps/worker`, `packages/shared`.
- Backend flow: Controller → Service → Repository → Prisma → PostgreSQL.
- Frontend: feature folders; Server Components default; TanStack Query for server state.
- Share only browser-safe contracts in `packages/shared`.

## Business gates

- 7-day trial from registration; compute expiry dynamically from `trialStartedAt` / `trialEndsAt`.
- Post-trial users must not receive correct answers, indicators, or explanations from the API.
- Question management is admin-only.
- No payment provider in the initial release; keep subscription modules ready but empty of payment complexity.
- Web auth: HTTP-only cookies + CSRF (DEC-012); question bank requires auth (DEC-003); post-trial PDFs allowed (DEC-001); password reset via email (DEC-004).

## When unsure

Add or update an entry in `docs/19-decisions-and-assumptions.md` with status `NEEDS APPROVAL`. Do not invent product rules.
